(3516018, 485305, 14614, '<td valign="top">you commented on my last place finish a while back so I''ll return the favor (not the best of feelings, I can relate)<br/> <br/>I am struck by the irony of the cell phone theme &amp; the feel of the cell-photo quality of the shot -- the greens are also an interesting blend given USA use of "green" and shopping - I see the voters had trouble looking past the low resolution without some help in connecting to the topic and I confess, had I voted in this one, I may not have either.</td>', 'you commented on my last place finish a while back so I''ll return the favor (not the best of feelings, I can relate) I am struck by the irony of the cell phone theme & the feel of the cell-photo quality of the shot -- the greens are also an interesting blend given USA use of "green" and shopping - I see the voters had trouble looking past the low resolution without some help in connecting to the topic and I confess, had I voted in this one, I may not have either.', '2007-04-03 20:42:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3516247, 485371, 7743, '<td valign="top">*** Critique Club ***<br/> <br/>First impression: Strong landscape<br/> <br/>Composition:  I like the high position of the peaks but feel that there is too much in the foreground.  Including a little more of the sky and a little less grass I think would work better.  Also, because of the direction the girl is walking, I think it would have been better if she was walking into the frame rather than out of it.<br/> <br/>Exposure: Seems right in most places though some parts of the cliff and the sand along the path seems a bit bright.<br/> <br/>Impact: The strength of the cliffs is where I feel the impact of the image is coming from.  I think more impact could be obtained by not cropping so close to the peak on the left.  A lower angle may add to the impact as well.<br/> <br/>Remember, this is just one opinion.<br/> <br/>Colette</td>', '*** Critique Club *** First impression: Strong landscape Composition:  I like the high position of the peaks but feel that there is too much in the foreground.  Including a little more of the sky and a little less grass I think would work better.  Also, because of the direction the girl is walking, I think it would have been better if she was walking into the frame rather than out of it. Exposure: Seems right in most places though some parts of the cliff and the sand along the path seems a bit bright. Impact: The strength of the cliffs is where I feel the impact of the image is coming from.  I think more impact could be obtained by not cropping so close to the peak on the left.  A lower angle may add to the impact as well. Remember, this is just one opinion. Colette', '2007-04-03 22:06:36.000000', NULL, 0),
